# Git safety

- Inspect `git status` before making changes; preserve existing user and agent work.
- Never `reset --hard`, `clean -fd`, rebase, force-push, or discard changes without **explicit** approval.
- Do not modify unrelated files. Keep architectural work, dependency upgrades, and product features separable.
- Do **not** commit or push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not commit `.env`, credentials, local databases, `dist`/builds, map downloads, or `node_modules`.
- Do not invent or reconfigure remotes (this repo may have no GitHub remote yet).
- Do not modify the Artelier repository on disk or its remotes/branches from SIDEBURNS tasks.
- When commits are requested: follow the user’s commit protocol; keep messages focused on why; never `--no-verify` unless asked.
- Keep documentation synchronized when architectural boundaries change.
